    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><p><strong>Oldenborn Heritage.</strong> The branch that stayed in the dirt. Bone of the bedrock, slow blood, slow grudge. The land remembers your name and answers when you call.</p><p><em>“The world remembered old names. You answered.”</em></p><p><strong>Earthbound.</strong> You are the place-soul that put down roots and refused to be moved. Folks call you a stout one—dwarf, gnome, hill spirit, depending on the dialect. The truth is older than any of those words.</p><h3>Traits</h3><ul><li><p><strong>Creature Type.</strong> Humanoid (Fey).</p></li><li><p><strong>Size.</strong> Medium.</p></li><li><p><strong>Lineage Lean.</strong> Your lineage leans toward <strong>BOD (Body)</strong>—expressed primarily through Tier powers.</p></li><li><p><strong>Stoneborn.</strong> You reroll the lowest die on checks to resist being knocked prone or forcibly moved while you stand on natural ground.</p></li></ul>",
